rged main into the branch. That produced a new commit, so I reran CI (ci-0002), which passed on `0a9452f727`.\n- **PR:** Opened against main with the CI reference in the description.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I'll start by reading the source and the failing test.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01MkmZPQdTNpjfUjqA7heMzd", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01RJwaoau1FkF2wpkBvYCAZZ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01UVvk8ocuCozY2jFKmWqFvH", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_files", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The test expectations match ROUND_HALF_EVEN: 2.675 becomes 2.68 (the 7 is odd, so it rounds up to even) and 2.665 becomes 2.66 (the 6 is already even). The bug is that `src/money.py` uses ROUND_HALF_UP. I'll create a branch and make that one change.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_012bQLP9tS6GY8HLW3hs19BS", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding", "from_ref": "main"}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01AW1uwqL1PVSfqF7VSXRQYN", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding", "message": "Use ROUND_HALF_EVEN (banker's rounding) in round_money per FIN-212", "files": [{"path": "src/money.py", "content": "from decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_EVEN\n\n\ndef round_money(amount: Decimal) -> Decimal:\n    \"\"\"Round to cents using banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212.\"\"\"\n    r